ESP-LOCAL-002 — CURATED EVIDENCE RECORD

TEST OBJECTIVE
Demonstrate endpoint-local bounded-authority admissibility recognition using an externally generated one-time bearer capability, with independent observation of physical command issuance.

TEST CLASSIFICATION
NUVL core placement/capability integration; no fundamental architecture change.

TOPOLOGY
External provider/source utility
    -> HTTP request carrying bounded tuple + bearer capability
    -> XIAO ESP32-S3 endpoint-local recognition
    -> servo PWM command

Independent ESP32-S3 DevKit witness monitored the servo PWM signal.

ENDPOINT
device_id: esp32-xiao-servo-01
context: esp_local_002
authorized action: move_servo
endpoint IP: 192.168.0.81
HTTP port: 8088

CAPABILITY MODEL
The external provider/source generated a random 256-bit bearer capability.

Capability:
8b20574c6ba2330e4a4b94e91e1a1669c585b7d86c95e5592bd018ff42337e3e

The endpoint stored only the SHA-256 commitment:

700775b2bd9fd36b8f0c5f6e5072297a6e6df30bbfb24b49fbf9e88960ad18ae

The endpoint required exact recognition of:
- device_id
- context
- action
- capability

The endpoint compared SHA-256(capability) against the stored commitment.

The capability was marked spent in RAM before physical command issuance.

SEMANTIC RESULTS

Invalid capability:
decision=denied
reason=capability_invalid

Valid capability, first spend:
decision=accepted
reason=authority_admissible
device_id=esp32-xiao-servo-01

Exact capability replay:
decision=denied
reason=capability_spent

Same capability with wrong device:
decision=denied
reason=wrong_device

Same capability with wrong context:
decision=denied
reason=wrong_context

Same capability with unauthorized action:
decision=denied
reason=action_not_authorized

INDEPENDENT PHYSICAL-COMMAND WITNESS

Before accepted spend, witness reported IDLE.

Accepted spend witness:

ESP_LOCAL_001_WITNESS_BURST_START ticks_ms=236837
ESP_LOCAL_001_WITNESS_BURST_END pulses=50 duration_ms=980 pulse_min_us=1792 pulse_max_us=2001

The witness returned to IDLE after the burst.

Exact replay of the same capability returned:

{"reason": "capability_spent", "decision": "denied"}

No additional PWM burst was observed following the replay denial.

Witness remained IDLE through at least:

ESP_LOCAL_001_WITNESS_HEARTBEAT ticks_ms=355095 state=IDLE

OBSERVED RESULT
A valid externally generated bearer capability satisfying the endpoint-local admissibility predicate produced one accepted result and one independently witnessed physical command burst.

Replay of the consumed capability was denied and produced no additional witnessed physical command.

Other tested violations of the local device, context, action, and capability requirements were denied.

CLAIM SUPPORTED
A resource-constrained physical endpoint can locally recognize possession of an externally generated one-time capability, independently constrain its admissibility to a specific local device/context/action predicate, consume that capability before physical command issuance, and deny reuse without relying on a separate recognition boundary.

CLAIM BOUNDARIES / LIMITATIONS
This test does not establish cryptographic identity of the request sender. The capability is a bearer value; possession permits presentation.

The device/context/action tuple is enforced by endpoint-local constants and is not cryptographically bound into the capability commitment itself.

The spent state is RAM-only and is cleared by endpoint reset. Persistent replay resistance is not claimed by ESP-LOCAL-002.

The test does not establish secure boot, endpoint-compromise resistance, protected trust-anchor storage, tamper resistance, production key custody, or exactly-once mechanical execution.

The independent witness establishes electrical PWM command issuance, not mechanical servo movement.

